Pumpkin Bars
  --Claire Saffitz

Crust:
1 1/4 cups ap flour
1/3 c powdered sugar
1/2 tsp Diamond Crystal kosher salt
10 tbsp cold unsalted butter, cut into 1/4" dice 

Line 8x8" pan with parchment paper (make sling). Preheat oven to 350F. Combine flour, sugar, and salt in a bowl. Add cubed butter and work with hands until butter is worked in pretty well. Once it sticks, can use spatula to really work it in until the dough is homogeneous. Press into the prepared pan, smooth as much as possible. Bake until really golden brown.

Filling:
1/2 c sugar + 2 tbsp water
1 c heavy cream, at room temperature
1 c pumpkin puree 
1/4 c brown sugar
2 tbsp room temp butter
Big pinch kosher salt
2 tsp vanilla
2 large eggs

Have all ingredients at room temp. Add water to the pan, then slowly pour sugar in the middle, turn on to medium high. Stir at the beginning to encourage the sugar to dissolve. Don't stir once it starts to steam. Looking to drive off all the water, can swirl pan if needed. Looking for dark caramel, have cream ready. Once ready, pull off heat and slowly add cream. Once combined, add butter, pumpkin, sugar, vanilla, salt, and whisk to combine. Then add eggs and continue to whisk. Keep warm until crust is ready to come out of the oven. Once crust is ready, pull from oven, pour filling over, and put back in oven, reducing temp to 325F. Bake until a little puffing around edges, and it jiggles, not sloshes (~20-25 min). Cool, then refrigerate to completely set before removing from pan and cutting.

Topping (optional)
1/3 c crème fraiche or mascarpone
2/3 c heavy cream

Whisk to combine and top over the chilled bars. Cut and serve.
